       "text": "Hand-painted watercolour storybook animation, loose dark-brown ink outlines, paper texture, warm daylight. The fox and the stork exactly as in the reference image. Static side-on camera at table height, medium-wide shot, the action kept in the centre of the frame. No dialogue, no text.\n\n0-7 s, the fox's dinner: a sunny garden with a low wooden table. The fox serves soup in two wide, flat, shallow plates. The fox happily finishes his plate; the stork taps at her flat plate with the tip of her long beak again and again but cannot eat any.\n\n7.5-15 s, the stork's dinner: a reed bed beside a pond. The stork serves dinner in two tall clay jars with long narrow necks. The stork reaches her long beak into her jar and eats happily; the fox sniffs at the narrow neck of his jar, cannot reach the food, and sits back disappointed, ears drooping."
